Subject: [PATCH] kconfig: keep the autoconf.h heading independent of the release

The C configuration header is an input to ccache's direct-mode manifest.
Keep its heading stable across kernel releases without changing configuration
definitions or the pound-style headings in .config and auto.conf.

--- a/scripts/kconfig/confdata.c
+++ b/scripts/kconfig/confdata.c
@@ -632 +632,4 @@ static void conf_write_heading(FILE *fp, const struct comment_style *cs)
-	fprintf(fp, "%s %s\n", cs->decoration, rootmenu.prompt->text);
+	if (cs == &comment_style_c)
+		fprintf(fp, "%s Linux Kernel Configuration\n", cs->decoration);
+	else
+		fprintf(fp, "%s %s\n", cs->decoration, rootmenu.prompt->text);
